  "description": "<p> </p>\r\n<p><span xss=removed>Tower Bridge is an iconic emblem of the nation’s capital. Flanked by two imposing structures, it commands the Thames that flows through the city and serves a continuous reminder of Britain’s historical significance. The Gamages Of London Limited Edition Hand Assembled Horace Capital Automatic Gold men’s watch celebrates its legacy and pays tribute to Sir Horace Jones, the architect that designed the bridge which was completed after his death.</span></p>\r\n<p><span xss=removed>The precise 163 part 21 jewel automatic movement operates similarly to the accurate system that raises and lowers the bridge for passing boats. This movement also ensures the Month, Date, Day, and Minutes functions, fixed into the crown-gold dial and complemented by luminous indices and hands, work with sublime dependability. The rotating gold bezel and gold inner ring add a royal industrial appeal that reminisces on the rich cultural significance of the Bridge itself.</span></p>\r\n<p><span xss=removed>The Gamages Of London logo engraved stainless steel caseback and gold stainless steel mesh bracelet bring the timepiece to completion, connecting the case the same way that Jones meant for Tower Bridge to link both sides of the river together in perpetuity.</span></p>",
